# Customer, product and inventory analytics

**Business question:** which customers retain and why, which products and categories deserve more space, and how should each node's assortment change?

> **Simulated data.** Everything comes from a seeded Python generator (`data_gen/generate.py`, seed {{ cfg.sim.seed }}), not from any real company. Assumptions: {{ cfg.sim.customers }} customers signing up through {{ cfg.sim.days }} days from {{ cfg.sim.start_date }} via five acquisition channels; Poisson ordering with a gamma-distributed personal rate while active and an exponential lifetime set by a monthly churn hazard; baskets of 1 + Poisson(4.8) lines, {{ (cfg.sim.repertoire_share * 100) | int }}% from a personal repertoire of {{ cfg.sim.repertoire_size }} favourite SKUs; {{ cfg.sim.n_skus }} SKUs in 15 categories ranged differently across {{ cfg.sim.n_nodes }} nodes; a six-step checkout funnel; daily order-up-to replenishment with FIFO ageing and write-off for perishables.

